(6949163, 1047799, 112739, '<td valign="top">From an old movie it feels like. What beautiful work. You should be proud of this image, hope is makes top 3.</td>', 'From an old movie it feels like. What beautiful work. You should be proud of this image, hope is makes top 3.', '2013-01-04 17:44:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949172, 1047736, 101256, '<td valign="top">A very gentle picture - about the only way I can describe it. Interesting how the pilings kind of fade into the distance. The little white "flare" in the middle of the pilings is rather distracting, although I know what caused that. A solid effort.</td>', 'A very gentle picture - about the only way I can describe it. Interesting how the pilings kind of fade into the distance. The little white "flare" in the middle of the pilings is rather distracting, although I know what caused that. A solid effort.', '2013-01-04 18:02:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949173, 1047231, 101256, '<td valign="top">A solid HDR type of image with two irritating flaws - the ghost branches on the left and right. The eye goes right to them which detracts from the over all impact of the image.</td>', 'A solid HDR type of image with two irritating flaws - the ghost branches on the left and right. The eye goes right to them which detracts from the over all impact of the image.', '2013-01-04 18:04:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949176, 1047844, 101256, '<td valign="top">Too little definition to make this an outstanding image and I think the conversion was over done.</td>', 'Too little definition to make this an outstanding image and I think the conversion was over done.', '2013-01-04 18:05:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949181, 1047732, 101256, '<td valign="top">I have in the past, and in other venues, complained mightly about the over use of the "flowing water" technique. It just seems to pedestrian - like sunrises and sunsets - everybody takes them and they happen often enough to become ordinary. In this case though, it wasn''t over used. The slight view of the creek bottom under the water flow is a plus and the overall impact is pleasing. A good job and a slightly different approach to a common technique.</td>', 'I have in the past, and in other venues, complained mightly about the over use of the "flowing water" technique. It just seems to pedestrian - like sunrises and sunsets - everybody takes them and they happen often enough to become ordinary. In this case though, it wasn''t over used. The slight view of the creek bottom under the water flow is a plus and the overall impact is pleasing. A good job and a slightly different approach to a common technique.', '2013-01-04 18:07:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949182, 1047715, 101256, '<td valign="top">From a technical standpoint, this is a very good capture. From an interest standpoint - meh.</td>', 'From a technical standpoint, this is a very good capture. From an interest standpoint - meh.', '2013-01-04 18:08:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949185, 1047666, 101256, '<td valign="top">I''ve looked and looked and looked at this and I just don''t like it. However, I''m not one to let personal opinion get in the way of a technically interesting image. Being fair is more important than personal opinion and from a technical standpoint, this is a great capture.</td>', 'I''ve looked and looked and looked at this and I just don''t like it. However, I''m not one to let personal opinion get in the way of a technically interesting image. Being fair is more important than personal opinion and from a technical standpoint, this is a great capture.', '2013-01-04 18:10:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949186, 1047662, 101256, '<td valign="top">I commented on an earlier entry that overuse of this technique was killing it as you see it improperly applied. This is one of those instances - there isn''t any definition to the water and it just blends together into a blue tinted mass - no interesting things to look at.</td>', 'I commented on an earlier entry that overuse of this technique was killing it as you see it improperly applied. This is one of those instances - there isn''t any definition to the water and it just blends together into a blue tinted mass - no interesting things to look at.', '2013-01-04 18:12:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949187, 1047632, 101256, '<td valign="top">TA DA!! The winner in this challenge I suspect. Very well done - excellent concept and execution. A beautiful still life.</td>', 'TA DA!! The winner in this challenge I suspect. Very well done - excellent concept and execution. A beautiful still life.', '2013-01-04 18:13:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949189, 1047760, 101256, '<td valign="top">Take this with a grain of salt if you will, but the reflected lights are very overpowering and distract from what could have been a very interesting image.</td>', 'Take this with a grain of salt if you will, but the reflected lights are very overpowering and distract from what could have been a very interesting image.', '2013-01-04 18:15:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949190, 1047835, 101256, '<td valign="top">I like this although I would have preferred a closer look and have shown off the reflection of the bridge a little more. Still, a very pleasing image.</td>', 'I like this although I would have preferred a closer look and have shown off the reflection of the bridge a little more. Still, a very pleasing image.', '2013-01-04 18:16:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949191, 1047658, 101256, '<td valign="top">You can tell this is a timed exposure as the fur on the sides of the cats are slightly blurred from their breathing patterns. I''m not much for cat photos - in fact, I''m not much of a cat person period (although there are two cats in the house, but they don''t belong to me - they belong to the Mrs.).  But, this has a very calming quality - nothing WOW about it, just a pleasing snapshot.</td>', 'You can tell this is a timed exposure as the fur on the sides of the cats are slightly blurred from their breathing patterns. I''m not much for cat photos - in fact, I''m not much of a cat person period (although there are two cats in the house, but they don''t belong to me - they belong to the Mrs.).  But, this has a very calming quality - nothing WOW about it, just a pleasing snapshot.', '2013-01-04 18:18:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949193, 1047856, 119863, '<td valign="top">A little bit more interesting than the usual abstract, greyscale entries I can make no sense of.</td>', 'A little bit more interesting than the usual abstract, greyscale entries I can make no sense of.', '2013-01-04 18:21:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949195, 1047451, 101256, '<td valign="top">Another great example of Modern Expressionism and the conversion is perfect. I''m sure this probably won''t score high, but I''m giving it a ten because it''s something that is right down the middle of the plate as far as I''m concerned.</td>', 'Another great example of Modern Expressionism and the conversion is perfect. I''m sure this probably won''t score high, but I''m giving it a ten because it''s something that is right down the middle of the plate as far as I''m concerned.', '2013-01-04 18:23:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949197, 1047838, 101256, '<td valign="top">I know that the intent was here and it sort of works, but there just isn''t any thing interesting to recommend it as a high score challenge image. I might have tried to use the green to halo the tree and use that as the image.</td>', 'I know that the intent was here and it sort of works, but there just isn''t any thing interesting to recommend it as a high score challenge image. I might have tried to use the green to halo the tree and use that as the image.', '2013-01-04 18:25:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6949199, 1047494, 101256, '<td valign="top">I hate to comment on images like this because if a little more thought had gone into it, it could have been a real contender - there is a lot of potential here - a little longer lens, maybe a different angle, different crop, etc.</td>', 'I hate to comment on images like this because if a little more thought had gone into it, it could have been a real contender - there is a lot of potential here - a little longer lens, maybe a different angle, different crop, etc.', '2013-01-04 18:27:07.000000', NULL, 1),
